.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-admin-onboardings-cancel - Delete a request that is not completed: its link stops working (write mode, audited)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 admin onboardings cancel  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete an onboarding request that is not completed: a mistaken invite, a sign-up that
should not go on. Its link stops working at once. It cannot be undone, but the merchant
can be invited again.

.PP
A completed request is history and is refused (422 onboarding_completed): to stop that
merchant, 'rail0 admin accounts deactivate' the account, whose id is the request's.

.PP
A write: it needs write mode ('rail0 admin write-mode on').


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for cancel

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip the confirmation prompt (required to run non-interactively)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 admin onboardings cancel 019f0c11-…
  rail0 admin onboardings cancel 019f0c11-… --yes
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-admin-onboardings(1)\fP
